        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "Second solution: It will be a bit more convenient to assume  $ P(0) = 1 $ (which we may achieve by rescaling unless  $ P(0) = 0 $, in which case there is nothing to prove) and to prove that there exists  $ D > 0 $ such that  $ \\int_{-1}^{1}|P(x)|dx \\geq D $, or even such that  $ \\int_{0}^{1}|P(x)|dx \\geq D $.",
          "block_bbox": [
            314,
            2188,
            1252,
            2440
          ],
          "block_id": 14,
          "block_order": 14,
          "group_id": 14,
          "block_polygon_points": [
