          ]
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "and  $ Q(x)(R(x)-kx) $ has more roots in [0, 1] than does P (and has the same value at 0). Repeating this argument shows that  $ \\int_{0}^{1}|P(x)|dx $ is greater than the corresponding integral for some polynomial with all of its roots in [0, 1].",
